---
// works.astro - Dedicated Works, System Blueprints & Engineering Case Studies
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Works & Systems Architecture — Mausam Kumar Giri"
  description="Production system case studies, architectural post-mortems, and engineering experiments by Mausam Kumar Giri. Payment orchestration, clinical EHRs, and WorldSkills topologies."
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-header">
      <span class="section-tag">ENGINEERING ARTIFACTS</span>
      <h1 class="section-title">Works & System Blueprints</h1>
      <p class="section-desc">
        Architectural breakdowns, failure prevention mechanisms, and technical post-mortems of systems engineered for production scale and international competition.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN WORKS LIST -->
    <div class="stories-list" style="margin-bottom: 5rem;">
      <!-- WORK 1: PAYMENTS -->
      <article class="story-item" id="payments">
        <div class="story-meta-bar">
          <span class="story-context">FINTECH ARCHITECTURE</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>MANTRACARE HEALTH</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>SYSTEM CASE STUDY</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="story-title">Multi-Provider Payment Orchestration Engine</h2>
        <p class="story-narrative">
          In a high-growth healthcare marketplace with patients booking doctor consultations globally, payment failures lead directly to abandoned care and lost revenue. Integrating a single payment processor leaves the platform vulnerable to gateway latency spikes, downtime during maintenance, and high currency conversion fees for international cards.
          <br /><br />
          <strong>The Solution:</strong> I built a decoupled payment routing engine that dynamically inspects transaction metadata (issuing country, currency, card scheme, transaction size) and dispatches to the optimal processor: <strong>Razorpay</strong> for UPI and Indian domestic transactions, <strong>Stripe Connect</strong> for US/EU multi-party marketplace splits, and <strong>Airwallex</strong> for competitive foreign exchange settlements.
        </p>

        <div class="story-pillars">
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">TRANSACTION INTEGRITY</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">Redis Distributed Locks & Idempotency</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">ASYNC RECONCILIATION</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">SQS Dead-Letter Queue Workers</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">RELIABILITY IMPACT</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">Zero Unreconciled State Discrepancies</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-card" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-secondary);">
          <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--accent-gold); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            CRITICAL FAILURE PREVENTION
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
            If an upstream webhook from Stripe or Razorpay drops due to network partitions, our automated worker queries the provider's ledger using exponential backoff, ensuring the patient's appointment is confirmed without requiring manual intervention.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- WORK 2: EHR & DIAGNOSTICS -->
      <article class="story-item" id="ehr">
        <div class="story-meta-bar">
          <span class="story-context">HEALTHCARE PLATFORMS</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>MANTRACARE HEALTH</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>SYSTEM CASE STUDY</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="story-title">Scalable EHR & Multi-Lab Diagnostic Automation</h2>
        <p class="story-narrative">
          Managing sensitive health records requires ironclad security without sacrificing doctor productivity. Practitioners needed flexible clinical templates supporting multi-lingual note entries, while patients needed automated pathology testing dispatched directly to national diagnostics labs.
          <br /><br />
          <strong>The Architecture:</strong> I designed the core EHR service handling over <strong>20,000 active patient profiles</strong>. The system incorporates granular Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), KMS envelope encryption for sensitive health fields, and bidirectional API dispatch pipelines directly integrated with <strong>Tata 1mg, Healthians, and Redcliffe Labs</strong> for automated phlebotomy home sample collection and pathology report syncing.
        </p>

        <div class="story-pillars">
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">DATA SCALE</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">20,000+ Encrypted Records</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">LAB PARTNER APIS</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">Tata 1mg • Healthians • Redcliffe</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">COMPLIANCE</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">HIPAA Data Isolation & Audit Logging</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- WORK 3: WORLDSKILLS -->
      <article class="story-item" id="worldskills">
        <div class="story-meta-bar">
          <span class="story-context">ARENA POST-MORTEM</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>GLOBAL SKILLS CHALLENGE AUSTRALIA</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>INTERNATIONAL GOLD</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="story-title">180-Minute High-Availability Cloud Deployment</h2>
        <p class="story-narrative">
          At the Global Skills Challenge in Wollongong, Australia (June 2026), international competitors were evaluated under strict real-time constraints. Tasks included building zero-trust VPC networks, auto-scaling EKS Kubernetes clusters, transit routing via AWS VPC Lattice, and disaster recovery execution under simulated region failure.
          <br /><br />
          <strong>The Execution:</strong> By leveraging modular, deterministic Terraform scripts and eliminating manual cloud console navigation, I completed the infrastructure build and verification tests with highest accuracy, earning the <strong>International Gold Medal in Cloud Computing</strong>.
        </p>

        <div class="story-pillars">
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">RESULT</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">1st Place — Gold Medalist</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">EVALUATION</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">High-Availability & Latency Benchmarks</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">METHOD</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">100% Declarative Terraform & Helm</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- WORK 4: NIT RESEARCH -->
      <article class="story-item" id="research">
        <div class="story-meta-bar">
          <span class="story-context">APPLIED AI RESEARCH</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>NIT KURUKSHETRA</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>RESEARCH PAPER / REPO</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="story-title">Cross-Domain Recommendation Model for Cold-Start Users</h2>
        <p class="story-narrative">
          Cold-start recommendation remains one of the hardest problems in machine learning. When a user has zero historical interactions, traditional collaborative filtering fails. During my research internship at NIT Kurukshetra, I explored transferring knowledge from dense auxiliary domains to sparse target domains using transformer architectures.
          <br /><br />
          I formulated an embedding projection pipeline that discovers semantic overlaps between disparate domains (e.g., book reviews to movie preferences), providing warm representations for cold-start entities.
        </p>

        <div class="story-pillars">
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">TECH STACK</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">Python, PyTorch, Transformers, Flask</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">EVALUATION</span>
            <span class="pillar-val">NDCG@10 & Hit-Rate Benchmarks</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar-item">
            <span class="pillar-label">OPEN SOURCE</span>
            <span class="pillar-val"><a href="https://github.com/mausam-giri/cross_recommendation_system" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-gold);">github.com/mausam-giri/cross_recommendation_system</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- THE ENGINEERING LAB (OPEN SOURCE & CRAFT) -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 5rem;">
      <div class="proof-header">
        <div>
          <span class="section-tag">OPEN SOURCE & EXPERIMENTS</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">The Engineering Lab</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Micro-innovations, UI stability fixes, and tools built to solve friction in daily workflows.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="proof-grid">
        <!-- Radix UI Fix -->
        <article class="proof-card">
          <div class="proof-card-top">
            <span class="medal-badge gold">OPEN SOURCE</span>
            <span class="proof-year">radix-ui</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="proof-card-title">Radix UI Layout Shift Fix (#1925)</h3>
          <div class="proof-card-sub">UI Engineering & Layout Stability</div>
          <p class="proof-card-body">
            Diagnosed and published CSS resolutions for cumulative layout shifts (CLS) triggered by scrollbar width recalculations in Radix UI Dialog and Select primitives.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/radix-ui/primitives/issues/1925" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="proof-verification">
            <span>View GitHub Issue & Fix</span> →
          </a>
        </article>

        <!-- LeadNear -->
        <article class="proof-card">
          <div class="proof-card-top">
            <span class="medal-badge gold">PRODUCT</span>
            <span class="proof-year">LeadNear</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="proof-card-title">LeadNear & Chrome Extension</h3>
          <div class="proof-card-sub">B2B Lead Intelligence Pipeline</div>
          <p class="proof-card-body">
            Engineered a high-speed Chrome extension interacting with LinkedIn DOM for verified B2B lead generation, parsing contact credentials and syncing with outreach databases.
          </p>
          <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/leadnear-b2b-email-phone/npofkafeajldomiogiiglkfebpnnaagn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="proof-verification">
            <span>Chrome Web Store Listing</span> →
          </a>
        </article>

        <!-- Pramman Patra -->
        <article class="proof-card">
          <div class="proof-card-top">
            <span class="medal-badge gold">CANVAS ENGINE</span>
            <span class="proof-year">Pramman Patra</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="proof-card-title">Pramman Patra Credential Canvas</h3>
          <div class="proof-card-sub">Digital Badge & Certificate Studio</div>
          <p class="proof-card-body">
            Designed an interactive SVG/HTML5 Canvas certificate studio allowing organizations to design, issue, and verify cryptographic digital credentials similar to Credly.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/mausam-giri/pramman-canvas-editor" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="proof-verification">
            <span>View Repository & Studio</span> →
          </a>
        </article>

        <!-- Real-Time Chat -->
        <article class="proof-card">
          <div class="proof-card-top">
            <span class="medal-badge gold">NETWORKING</span>
            <span class="proof-year">WebSockets</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="proof-card-title">Low-Latency Django WebSockets</h3>
          <div class="proof-card-sub">Real-Time Messaging Protocol</div>
          <p class="proof-card-body">
            Built an asynchronous WebSocket messaging engine in Django with message delivery receipts, online presence telemetry, and minimal server memory overhead.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/mausam-giri/Friends-DjangoChat" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="proof-verification">
            <span>View Repository</span> →
          </a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
